# Environment variables.
#
# .env carried the Gemini key for the Python application that used to live
# here. The edge Worker takes its secrets from `wrangler secret put` and, for
# local development, from edge/.dev.vars -- both ignored below. The wildcard
# covers every other variant someone might create later.
.env
.env.*

# Credentials and keys.
#
# Deny-by-default: every .json is ignored, and the few that are genuinely safe
# to publish are named below. The Firebase Admin SDK service-account key is a
# .json and grants full administrative access to the project, so the blanket
# rule is the point of this section - do not replace it with a named pattern.
*.json
# Firebase project configuration - identifies the project, holds no secret.
!firebase.json
!firestore.indexes.json
!database.rules.json
# Node manifests. The lockfile is committed so `npm ci` reproduces the exact
# tree that the Firestore rules suite was verified against.
!package.json
!package-lock.json
# Frozen test data. The parity references were produced by the Python
# implementation that is no longer in this repository, and the bench manifests
# describe fixture images that are no longer generated -- so both are source
# now, not output. Neither holds a secret.
!edge/tests/reference/*.json
!bench/manifest_*.json
# The formula recogniser's vocabulary. It sits beside the two .onnx files in
# edge/build/mfr-int8/ and is as much a part of that model as they are --
# without it `npm run build:models` cannot rebuild public/models/mfr. The
# deny-by-default rule above was hiding it.
!edge/build/mfr-int8/tokenizer.json

# Certificates and private keys in any other form.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt

# Python. Only edge/tools/build-mfr.py remains, and it is run by hand to
# rebuild the formula recogniser's weights.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# IDEs
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Node
node_modules/

# Cloudflare/Wrangler local files. Keep edge source visible to Git.
edge/.dev.vars
edge/.wrangler/
edge/node_modules/

# Test output: screenshots, probe scripts, built PDFs.
edge/tests/out/

# Firebase CLI local state: emulator data, deploy caches and debug logs.
.firebase/
*.log
